Mind, that's not reliable. But a very good weapon for a rogue.

> [...] My max HP is 109, max power is 52.
> Stats: St: 18/24 Dx: 18 Co: 20 (due to a +2 ring) In: 9 Wi: 12 Ch 10
> 
> [...] I have poison, cold, and
> fire resistances, plus automatic searching. [...]

For your planned ascension (and even before) having MR is a must.

> I have Grimtooth (unenchanted at the moment, but I do have enchant
> weapon scrolls identified and will get it enchanted once I find a
> magic marker) and 11 +6 blessed orcish daggers, as well as 15 blessed
> regular daggers as backup.

My suggestion would be to enchant Stormbringer, wield Grimtooth
while walking, switch to Stormbringer with the 'x' command when
fighting melee, then immediately switch back after the fight.

> I got incredibly lucky with my armor (and
> am hoping the RNG isn't going to make me pay for it later), and
> managed to score a +5 cloak of invisibility (which I have fireproofed)
> and a +5 orcish helm (which I have rustproofed).

Fooproofing those pieces of armor, if done with an enchant armor
scroll, is a waste of that scroll; it's better spent on a yet
unenchanted piece of armor, or saved for the dragon scales that
you should strive to acquire.

> I also have blessed
> +2 dwarvish mithril, some +1 jackboots, and some nonmagical gloves.
> coupled with some blessings I got for generous donations, I have a -20
> AC

As said, get some dragon scale mail, and it would be nice to have
some speed boots as well.

> I also was incredibly lucky with a wand of polymorph and managed to
> change my pet dog into a lich, which has sense become a level 26 arch-
> lich with invisibility, 201 HP, and a -16 AC

Uh-oh! Had that too, recently, and it was annoying.

> Other equipment:
> [...]
> Copious numbers of offensive wands, plus a few wands of digging,
> teleportation, polymorph, create monster, enlightenment, and a few
> unidentified ones

You can identify many of the wands; scribble some text in the dust
with your fingers, then engrave with the wand.

> Water walking boots

I'd probably wear those on watery levels, even if you lose 2 points
of AC; too often I stumbled into a moat.

> Stormbringer (which I'm not using because I have no experience with
> longswords,

It belongs to the rune-sword class, which actually are broadswords,
not longswords.

> plus I don't want to accidentally anger my pet arch-lich.
> I'm keeping it to either sell or enhance my score)

I'd primarily use it as weapon in melee; it's the best weapon you
have, besides your stack of daggers, and one of the best existing.

> [...] once I can get some GDSM (aka: the protection from YASD)

Ah, okay, you know. :-)

> 8 potions of holy water, a blessed potion of gain level (which I'm
> going to quaff once I level up normally to maximize its effect),

Hmm.. - there are much better applications for those potions, for
characters who plan to ascend.

> [...]
> cursed ring of searching, [...]

Try to uncurse it and wear it; it helps to reduce the probability
to stumble in a a polymorph trap that may destroy your armor.

> Blessed luckstone from gnomish mines (those work even if they're in
> your bag of holding, right?)

No, wrong. They work only if carried in open inventory.

> Copious numbers of unidentified gems, a good number of which are
> probably valuable

You can identify wothless glass easily by throwing them to a unicorn
and observing the messages. Then drop that worthless weight.

> 13,059 zorkmids

Buy as much protection as possible as long as you are low level; you
can get 9 points of intrinsic protection easily. The rest of the gold
is just useless weight after you've visited all shops. In the late game
you need just a few bucks to bribe some demons.

> So here are my questions: First of all, do I have a descent chance of
> ascending?

Yes, but having MR is crucial! You have practically no chance without.

> Second, should I raid Fort Ludios before I do my quest or after?

For Ludios you should have reflection; don't do it without. (An option
could be wielding a cockatrice.) I'd do Ludios only in case I'd need
gold, which you don't seem to need, or dragon armor, but there I'd
prefer to first seek in the Castle.

> And third, is there anything else I should do that will help me
> out at this point?

I think I've mentioned the primary short term goals.

